W: 1. Noo summer days and heather bells
W: Come reakin owre yon hieland hills,
W: There's yellow corn in yonder fields
W: And autumn brings the shearin'.
W:
W: Chorus:
W: O, bonnie lassie, will ye gang
W: And shear wi' me the haie day lang?
W: And love will cheer us as we gang
W: To join yon band o' shearers.
W:
W: 2. And if the thistle it be strang,
W: And if it jags your milk white hand,
W: It's wi' my hook i'll cut it doon,
W: hen we join yon band o' shearers.
W:
W: 3. And if the weather it be hot,
W: I'll cast my waistcoat and my coat,
W: And shear wi' you amang the lot,
W: When we join the band o' shearers.
W:
W: 4. And if the weather it be dry,
W: They'll say there's love 'tween you and I,
W: But we'll siyiy pass each other by
W: When we join the band ot shearers.
W:
W: 5. And when the harvest is all done,
W: We'll hae some rantin' rovin' fun,
W: We'll hae some rantin' rovin' fun
W: And forget the toils o' shearing.
%
